 ~
 >speech_prog one 1~
  if quest(0,5,$n) == 20
  say Very good! Your mind is quick, you would be surprised at
  say how many fail that test of wisdom!
  mpoload 27724
  mpquiet on
  cast 'remove curse'
  mpquiet off
  give i27724 $n
  mpjunk i27724
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 0
  say Congratulations, you have passed all the tests
  say in our fair land.
  say Enjoy your stay here.
  say I will take you back to the square. You don't want
  say to get mugged on your way.
  mpechoat $n $i takes you to the square and returns home.
  mpechoaround $n $i and $n leave $i's house.
  mptransfer $n 27700
  mpgoto 27700
  mpgoto 27755
  mpecho $i returns safely home.
  else
  say One what? One resident here? One house? One life to lose? What?
  endif
 ~
 >speech_prog ~
  if quest(0,5,$n) == 20
   cackle
   mpmset $n quest 0 5 21
   say You have made me a wealthy man indeed.
   say Your answer was incorrect and now Bidanggu is required to
   say pay me for your loss. He bet me.....
   mpecho Ganngalida stands and thinks for a moment.
   say No, I'll let him tell you.
   snicker
   say Go see him and tell him "Another failure coming to see you."
   say Now leave me to my thoughts, failure.
   mpecho Ganngalida waves his hand and.....
   mptransfer $n 27799
  endif
 ~
 >speech_prog p Garrawa sent me~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 17
  say He did, did he?
  say Now why would he do a thing like that?
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 19
  else
  say Somehow, I doubt it.
 endif
 ~
 >speech_prog test wisdom riddle~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 19
  say Ohhh, yes, I like these times! Most people around here
  say don't want to stretch their minds.
  tell $n As I was on my way to Chakkor,
  mpechoaround $n {030}$i says 'If you added all the homes in this city'{300}
  tell $n I met a woman with nine bags.
  mpechoaround $n {030}$i says 'and included the number of different streets'{300}
  tell $n Inside each bag were nine cats.
  mpechoaround $n {030}$i says 'dividing that number by the number of guildhouses'{300}
  tell $n Each cat had nine kittens.
  mpechoaround $n {030}$i says 'and multiplied it by the number of stores in Chakkor'{300}
  tell $n Each kitten was playing with two mice.
  mpechoaround $n {030}$i says 'what total would you have?'{300}
  mpechoat $n {030}$i asks you 'How many were on their way to Chakkor?'
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 20
 else
  say What are you mumbling about, $n?
 endif
