 #27713
 Yannyalu~
 Yannyalu~
 Yannyalu sits here, discussing simple matters whith anyone who will listen.
 ~
 She is quite old and poor, although it is obvious she has taken great care of
 herself. A widow of a great many years, she depends on the kindness of others
 for her sustenance. Her clothes, neat but worn out, her speech simple yet
 complex, her eyes old yet piercing to the heart, she speaks of a great simple
 wisdom lost to the citizens within her own community. Their folly could well be
 your gain.
 ~
 ACT_BODY|ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_NO_ORDER|ACT_STAY_AREA|ACT_IS_NPC|ACT_RACE
 AFF_UNDERSTAND|AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_SANCTUARY|AFF_PROTECT_EVIL|AFF_PROTECT_GOOD|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN
 1000 S
 50 BODY_MOUTH|BODY_HEAD BODY_FOOT|BODY_HIP 1d100+1250 3d5+40
 10000 RACE_GNOME
 POS_RESTING POS_RESTING SEX_FEMALE
 >all_greet_prog 100~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 5 
    say Ahh, yes.
    say Yangal told me to expect you.
    smile $n
 else 
    if quest(0,5,$n) == 8
       cackle $n
       say You thought you could out wit me, leave!
       mpechoat $n Wow! That made your head spin!
       mpechoaround $n $n is thrown out of $i's house by some unseen force.
       mptransfer $n 27725
    endif
 endif
 ~
 >speech_prog star~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 7
    say Well, you ARE smarter than you look.
    mpecho Yannyalu lets out a sigh.
    say I guess I will have to let go of this bracelet,
    say you deserve it.
    mpoload 27726
    mpquiet
    cast 'remove curse'
    mpquiet off
    give i27726 $n
    mpjunk i27726
    mpmset $n quest 0 5 10
    tell $n Now, I will tell you who I gave the other two
    tell $n items too. I am sure like me, he will be willing
    tell $n to part with the eq if you prove yourself to him.
    tell $n Go see Ganalanja. Tell him I told you I gave him
    tell $n two worthless items.
    tell $n Good luck.
    mpechoat $n You saunter out of $i's home with a sense of great accomplisment.
    mpechoaround $n $n's face seems to glow with pride as $e leaves.
    mptransfer $n 27725
 endif
 ~
 >speech_prog ~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 7
    say Well well well!
    say You don't look that smart and a reply like that proves it!
    mpmset $n quest 0 5 8
    pat $n
    tell $n Well this is great!  I had a bet with Bidanggu
    tell $n that I would fool you. Go to Bidanggu and say 'another
    tell $n failure coming to see you' and I will let you try again.
    pat $n
    say Now leave my home.
    mpechoat $n You sadly make your departure.
    mpechoaround $n $n leaves $i's house, seemingly with $l tail between $l legs.
    mptransfer $n 27725
 endif
 ~
 >speech_prog p Yangal told me she gave you some items she found in the trash.~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 5
    say Ahh, yes she did.
    say She gave me a bracelet, a pair of gloves, and a pair of boots.
    say I only kept the bracelet and gave the other two items to another
    say close friend. I am willing to part with my bracelet if you can
    say correctly answer a question.
    say Do you wish to take my challenge?
    mpmset $n quest 0 5 6
 endif
 ~
 >speech_prog yes~
 if quest(0,5,$n) == 6
    say Great!  My husband was once a great farmer, let him rest in peace.
    say He wasn't a stupid farmer, one year he was given 10 apple trees.
    tell $n Somehow he planted all 10 trees in 5 rows.
    tell $n But, the mysterious thing was that each row
    tell $n had 4 trees in them!
    say What did our field look like that year?
    mpmset $n quest 0 5 7
 endif
